<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-3">3 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Meiji Restoration returns power to Japan's emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Choshu</a> seized the imperial palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> and an imperial decree abolished the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a>. The young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji">Emperor Meiji</a>'s government launched <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s rapid modernisation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji">Emperor Meiji</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-16">16 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Johnson escapes conviction by one vote</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate voted 35 to 19 to convict President Johnson on the first article tried, one vote short of the two-thirds needed. Johnson was the first US president to be impeached.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-26">26 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Last public hanging takes place in England</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Michael Barrett, convicted of the Clerkenwell bombing, was hanged before a crowd outside Newgate Prison. Three days later a new Act moved executions inside prison walls.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-23">23 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Latham Sholes patents a typewriter</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Sholes and his partners received a patent for a 'Type-Writer'. Developed further and sold by Remington, it popularised the QWERTY keyboard and transformed office work.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-9">9 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The 14th Amendment wins enough states for ratification</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>'s and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>'s approval gave the 14th Amendment the three-quarters of states it needed. It guaranteed citizenship to all born in the US and equal protection of the laws.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-28">28 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The 14th Amendment is certified as part of the US Constitution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State William Seward certified the 14th Amendment, guaranteeing citizenship and equal protection of the laws. It became the basis for many landmark civil rights rulings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-18">18 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Solar eclipse observations reveal the element later named helium</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Observing a total solar eclipse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Jules Janssen saw an unexplained yellow line in the Sun's spectrum. Norman Lockyer attributed it to a new element, helium, not found on Earth until 1895.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-3">3 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Willis Menard becomes the first African American elected to Congress</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Menard, a poet born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaskaskia">Kaskaskia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> parents, was elected to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> House of Representatives after moving to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>. His opponent contested the result, and opposition kept him from being seated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-27">27 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Custer's troops attack Black Kettle's camp on the Washita</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 7th Cavalry under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-armstrong-custer">George Armstrong Custer</a> attacked a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a> village on the Washita River, killing Black Kettle and many women and children. The army called it a battle; many historians call it a massacre.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-toba-fushimi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-toba-fushimi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-toba-fushimi">Battle of Toba–Fushimi</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Toba–Fushimi, fought from 27 to 31 January 1868 south of Kyoto, opened the Boshin War in Japan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain">Glorious Revolution (Spain)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Glorious Revolution of September 1868 was a military rising led by Generals Juan Prim and Francisco Serrano and Admiral Juan Bautista Topete that drove Queen Isabella II of Spain into exile.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/grito-de-lares">Grito de Lares</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Grito de Lares was an uprising against Spanish rule in Puerto Rico on 23 September 1868, planned by Ramón Emeterio Betances from exile.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fort-laramie-1868" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fort-laramie-1868.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fort-laramie-1868">Treaty of Fort Laramie (1868)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Fort Laramie of 1868 was an agreement between the United States and bands of the Lakota, Yanktonai Dakota and Arapaho that ended Red Cloud's War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
