<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/empire-of-japan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Empire%20of%20Japan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Empire of Japan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Meiji Restoration overthrows the Tokugawa shogunate after some 265 years</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tokugawa-shogunate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tokugawa%20Shogunate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tokugawa Shogunate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Imperial rule is restored and the Boshin War begins at Toba-Fushimi</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/principality-of-liechtenstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Principality%20of%20Liechtenstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Principality of Liechtenstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Prince Johann II abolishes the army</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/bahai-faith"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bah%C3%A1'%C3%AD%20Faith.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bahá'í Faith</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bahá’u’lláh is exiled to the Ottoman prison city of Acre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/shinto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Shinto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Shinto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Meiji government orders the separation of kami and buddhas</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/navajo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Navajo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Navajo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Bosque Redondo lets the surviving Navajo return to a reservation on part of their former homeland</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/meiji-restoration"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Meiji%20Restoration.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Meiji Restoration</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Domain troops seize the Imperial Palace and the Emperor declares the restoration of his authority, setting off the Boshin War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/emperor-meiji"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Emperor%20Meiji.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Emperor Meiji</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The restoration of imperial rule is proclaimed, the Charter Oath is issued and Edo is renamed Tokyo</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/tao-te-ching"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tao%20Te%20Ching.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tao Te Ching</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">John Chalmers publishes the first English translation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/samarkand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Samarkand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Samarkand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Russian forces under General von Kaufman take the citadel</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-little-bighorn"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Little%20Bighorn.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Little Bighorn</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The valley becomes part of the new Crow Indian Reservation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/the-canterbury-tales"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/The%20Canterbury%20Tales.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>The Canterbury Tales</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">F. J. Furnivall identifies nine Groups of tales under the auspices of the Chaucer Society</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/moai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Moai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Moai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The moai Hoa Hakananai'a was removed from the island; it is now in the British Museum</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sitting-bull"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sitting%20Bull.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sitting Bull</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gall and other Hunkpapa sign the Treaty of Fort Laramie; Sitting Bull does not agree to it</span></li></ul></section>
